# Add A and B Axis

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

`aaxis:` and `baxis:` maps on the `Carpet` trace configure the parametric axis labels.
`tickprefix:`/`ticksuffix:` annotate tick values. `smoothing: 1` curves the grid lines.
`minorgridcount: 9` adds 9 minor grid subdivisions between each major tick.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Carpet}

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Carpet.new(
    a: [4, 4, 4, 4.5, 4.5, 4.5, 5, 5, 5, 6, 6, 6],
    b: [1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3],
    y: [2, 3.5, 4, 3, 4.5, 5, 5.5, 6.5, 7.5, 8, 8.5, 10],
    aaxis: %{
      tickprefix: "a = ",
      ticksuffix: "m",
      smoothing: 1,
      minorgridcount: 9
    },
    baxis: %{
      tickprefix: "b = ",
      ticksuffix: "Pa",
      smoothing: 1,
      minorgridcount: 9
    }
  )
)
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "Carpet Plot — A and B Axes")
|> Plotly.show()
```
